=== Approval checkpoint: requirements ===
Output: {normalized_spec=Extend the existing URL shortener service to allow authenticated users to optionally specify a custom alias (short code) when creating a shortened URL, instead of relying on the system's auto-generated code. The system must validate the alias for allowed characters, length constraints, and uniqueness against existing short codes before accepting it, returning a clear error if the alias is invalid or already taken. If no custom alias is provided, the existing auto-generation logic should continue to be used. Non-functional requirements include maintaining current performance and availability characteristics of the shortening endpoint and ensuring alias validation does not introduce race conditions under concurrent creation requests., assumptions=[The existing system already has a mechanism to check short code uniqueness that can be reused or extended for custom aliases, Custom alias creation is restricted to authenticated users, consistent with how other write operations are handled, Allowed characters for aliases will follow common conventions (alphanumeric, hyphens, underscores) unless otherwise specified, There is an existing data store for URL mappings that can accommodate custom aliases without schema changes beyond minor additions], open_ambiguities=[What are the exact allowed length and character set constraints for custom aliases?, Should custom aliases be case-sensitive or case-insensitive when checking uniqueness?, Is there a reserved word list (e.g., admin, api) that should be excluded from allowed aliases?, Should there be rate limiting or quotas on how many custom aliases a single user can create?, Can existing auto-generated short codes be reused as custom aliases by other users, or should they remain permanently reserved?]}
