=== Approval checkpoint: design ===
Output: {api_contract=Extend the existing POST /api/urls (or equivalent shorten endpoint) in shortener-service/controller to accept an optional 'customAlias' field in the request body alongside the target URL, requiring authentication (existing auth middleware/token check). On success, return 201 with the shortened URL using the custom alias or auto-generated code as before. On invalid or taken alias, return 400 (invalid format/length/characters) or 409 (alias already exists) with a clear error message and error code distinguishing the two cases. No new endpoints are introduced; existing GET /{code} redirect endpoint remains unchanged., data_model=Extend the existing URL mapping entity (shortener-service/model) with no structural changes beyond ensuring the short_code field can store either auto-generated or user-supplied values, plus an optional is_custom boolean flag (or equivalent) to distinguish alias origin for future auditing/quota needs. A unique constraint/index on short_code remains the enforcement point for uniqueness, now shared by both generation paths., short_code_strategy=When customAlias is provided, validate it against character set (alphanumeric, hyphens, underscores), length bounds, and reserved-word exclusions before insertion; if valid, attempt to persist it using the same uniqueness-checking mechanism as auto-generated codes. If no alias is provided, fall back unchanged to the existing auto-generation algorithm. This reuses existing infrastructure rather than introducing a new generation path, minimizing risk to current behavior., caching_strategy=Deferred — no changes to the existing redirect caching mechanism are required by this feature; custom aliases are stored and looked up through the same data path as auto-generated codes, so current caching behavior for the redirect endpoint remains unaffected.}
